  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe tool library window drew a thread mill as a large plain cylinder. The 3D model and the side view used `Tool::profile`. That profile is the crest cylinder over the full cutting length, because the reach laws read that envelope (#894).\n\n- New display-only module `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_library_dialog/thread_form.rs`. It draws the cutting length of a thread mill as its teeth:\n  - the core at the tooth roots: the crest radius minus the external ISO root depth (`EXTERNAL_DEPTH_PER_PITCH` x pitch);\n  - one V tooth of the stated form angle for each row: `thread_mill::rows` rows on a multi-form mill, one tooth over the stated tooth height on a single-form mill;\n  - the steel above the cutting length stays: the shank of `Tool::profile`, or the neck of a landed drawn cutter.\n- `model.rs` calls `thread_form::toothed` on the steel outline (one line). The 3D mesh and the side view of the window both read that outline.\n- Every point stays inside the crest cylinder, so the plain mesh's box does not change.\n- A thread mill has no neck field: a neck comes from the drawn cutter outline (`thread_mill.rs`). The PR keeps that model. The decision is in `docs/decisions/4451-thread-mill-preview.md`.\n\nDisplay only. `Tool::profile`, the collision envelope, toolpaths, simulation and posted output do not change. No command changes, so no MCP tool is necessary.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nIn `camcraft-ui` lib, `egui_app::tool_library_dialog::thread_form::tests`:\n\n- `a_multi_form_thread_mill_draws_one_tooth_per_row_on_its_core` (8 crests at the cutting diameter, the roots at the core, the teeth end on the core at the cutting length)\n- `a_single_form_thread_mill_draws_one_tooth_then_its_neck` (one tooth, then a drawn 4 mm neck keeps its diameter and length, then the shank)\n- `the_profile_shank_follows_the_teeth`\n- `other_kinds_and_bad_numbers_draw_no_teeth`\n\n## Gate (head `b20e12ace`, winbuild)\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 10 steps, 0 failed (ui lib and 8 ui suites by the gate map).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The 4 pinning tests: 4 passed (`cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib thread_form`).\n- `crates/ui` `#[test]` count: 2009 before, 2013 after.\n- No post or toolpath changes, so the example catalog suites do not apply. The light lane was not run: the diff reaches no heavy lane (ui only).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The Properties side preview (`tool_preview::paint` without a steel override) still draws the crest cylinder. #4452 (flutes for each kind, a finer mesh, separate colours) can call `thread_form::toothed` there.\n- Thread mills with a landed drawn cutter were tested in the unit test only, not in a render.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nMulti-form thread mill, 8 mm, pitch 1.25, 12 mm cutting length, 3D view (holder off):\n\n| before | after |\n|---|---|\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4458/before-multi-3d.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4458/after-multi-3d.png) |\n\nSide view, multi-form:\n\n| before | after |\n|---|---|\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4458/before-multi-side.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4458/after-multi-side.png) |\n\nSingle-form thread mill, 8 mm, 2 mm tooth, 3D and side views:\n\n| before | after |\n|---|---|\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4458/before-single-3d.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4458/after-single-3d.png) |\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4458/before-single-side.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4458/after-single-side.png) |\n\nEffort: medium (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: The tool library preview draws the teeth of a thread mill on its cutting length, not a plain cylinder (#4451).\n\nFixes #4451\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
